<!--
  modules/ui_data/pom.xml — Stage 2-f Task 4 module POM (Wave D)
  (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-stage2f-remaining-modules.md).

  STATUS: ADDITIVE and RUN BY HAND (mvn -pl modules/ui_data -am package from
  the reactor root, or mvn -f modules/ui_data/pom.xml package). Ant
  (modules/ui_data/build.xml + build.incl.xml) remains the real build;
  nothing here is wired into CMake or any release build yet.

  WHY THIS MODULE. Part of Wave D — four modules whose only unmigrated-wave
  dependency was gui (Wave C, now in the reactor). ui_data is the largest of
  the four (146 source files: the variable browser/editor, the file browser,
  the news feed panel, and their datatable/rowheader/celleditor/renderer/undo
  support) and, despite its size, the CLEANEST dependency-wise of this wave —
  six reactor dependencies and, uniquely among this wave's four modules, NO
  vendored third-party jar at all.

  STEP 1 FINDINGS (./maven-module-deps.sh ui_data, 146 files):
    [1] imports (excluding ui_data's own packages): org.scilab.modules.
        action_binding{,.highlevel,.highlevel.ScilabInterpreterManagement},
        commons{,.gui}, graphic_objects.graphicObject, gui.bridge.
        {checkboxmenuitem,contextmenu,filechooser,menuitem,tab,toolbar,
        window}, gui.checkboxmenuitem, gui.console, gui.contextmenu,
        gui.events.callback, gui.menu, gui.menubar, gui.menuitem,
        gui.messagebox{,.ScilabModalDialog}, gui.tab, gui.tabfactory,
        gui.textbox, gui.toolbar, gui.utils, gui.window, localization,
        types, plus a static import of action_binding.highlevel.
        ScilabInterpreterManagement.asynchronousScilabExec — six reactor
        dependencies, all below (all already migrated: Wave C for gui,
        earlier waves for the rest). org.w3c.dom is JDK (java.xml module),
        not a dependency. No third-party (non-org.scilab, non-JDK) import
        anywhere in this module's 146 files.
    [2] reflection targets — RULED OUT: org.scilab.modules.scinotes.
        SciNotes, reached only via filebrowser/actions/
        OpenFileInSciNotesAction.java:49's inline
        `Class.forName("org.scilab.modules.scinotes.SciNotes")` (confirmed
        by reading the file — a try/catch around Class.forName + reflective
        method lookup, not an import). scinotes is Wave E, nowhere near
        migrated — reproduced as an absence, the same pattern
        modules/console/pom.xml's HelpSearchField finding and
        modules/history_browser/pom.xml's EditInScinotesAction finding both
        follow. This particular call site — an INLINE string literal
        directly inside Class.forName(...) — is exactly the shape [2]'s
        regex is built to catch, and it did; cross-checked anyway with an
        independent `grep -rn 'Class\.forName\|loadClass('` sweep of all 146
        files (one further hit, the same OpenFileInSciNotesAction.java call
        site — nothing missed). See modules/history_browser/pom.xml's header
        for the CONTRASTING case this tool structurally cannot catch
        (Class.forName(A_CONSTANT_VARIABLE)), found elsewhere in this same
        wave — not a live concern here, since ui_data's one reflective call
        is already the inline shape the tool sees.
    [3] fully-qualified uses with no import: org.scilab.modules.graph.
        actions.base.DefaultAction — RULED OUT, and worth spelling out
        because ui_data ALSO defines its own actions.DefaultAction (a
        completely different class: org.scilab.modules.ui_data.actions.
        DefaultAction extends CommonCallBack, imported directly and used
        throughout this module, e.g. variablebrowser/actions/
        CloseAction.java). The graph.actions.base.DefaultAction spelling
        appears exactly once, in actions/FilteringAction.java:34's `@see
        org.scilab.modules.graph.actions.base.DefaultAction#actionPerformed
        (java.awt.event.ActionEvent)` — a javadoc `@see` tag pointing at
        graph's unrelated same-named class for documentation purposes only,
        not code (confirmed by reading the file). graph is this same Wave D,
        so even a real dependency here would not have crossed a wave
        boundary — but it is not a real dependency: ui_data's own [1] import
        list never mentions org.scilab.modules.graph at all, and the single
        [3] hit is inert javadoc. graph is correctly NOT one of this
        module's <dependencies> below. Every other name in this category
        (action_binding.InterpreterManagement, commons.{CommonFileUtils,OS,
        ScilabConstants}, commons.gui.*, graphic_objects.graphicObject.
        CallBack, the sixteen gui.* classes, localization.Messages,
        types.{ScilabTypeEnum,ScilabTypeEnumDescription}) is already covered
        by the six reactor dependencies below, nothing new.
  No manifest.class-path anywhere in build.xml (confirmed again in the
  Ant-built jar's manifest: Class-Path is the literal, never-interpolated
  string "${manifest.class-path}").

  IMPLEMENTATION-VERSION: present, frozen at the literal "00000000 0000",
  positioned between Implementation-Title and Implementation-Vendor exactly
  where Ant's own jar places it (confirmed against modules/ui_data/jar/
  org.scilab.modules.ui_data.jar's actual manifest before extraction: live
  value there was "20260719 1729", a DSTAMP/TSTAMP pair). Vendor string
  double-encoded ("Ã¨", bytes c3 83 c2 a8) — extracted, never retyped, same
  as every other module.
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
    <artifactId>scilab-modules-parent</artifactId>
    <version>2027.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>ui_data</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>

  <!-- build.xml:19 <property name="library.title" value="User interface graphical components"/> -->
  <name>User interface graphical components</name>

  <dependencies>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.action_binding.InterpreterManagement,
         action_binding.highlevel.ScilabInterpreterManagement (also via a
         static import of its asynchronousScilabExec method). -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>action_binding</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.commons.{CommonFileUtils, OS, ScilabConstants},
         commons.gui.{FindIconHelper, ScilabGUIUtilities, ScilabKeyStroke,
         ScilabLAF}. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>commons</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.graphic_objects.graphicObject.CallBack. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>graphic_objects</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.gui.* — sixteen classes across bridge.
         {checkboxmenuitem,contextmenu,filechooser,menuitem,tab,toolbar,
         window}, checkboxmenuitem, console, contextmenu, events.callback,
         menu, menubar, menuitem, messagebox, tab, tabfactory, textbox,
         toolbar, utils, window — this module's UI panels are all gui
         bridge/Swing widgets underneath. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>gui</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.localization.Messages — the ordinary
         reactor-sibling idiom used across nearly every module. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>localization</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- org.scilab.modules.types.{ScilabTypeEnum,
         ScilabTypeEnumDescription} — the variable browser/editor's data
         model. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>types</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <!-- build.incl.xml:22 <property name="src.dir" location="src/java/"/>.
         Same source tree Ant compiles — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
         identical comment; nothing module-specific to add here. -->
    <sourceDirectory>src/java</sourceDirectory>

    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <archive>
            <!-- addMavenDescriptor=false and the Built-By entry are
                 inherited from the parent POM — not redeclared here. Same
                 manifestFile mechanism as modules/localization/pom.xml (see
                 that file's build comment for the full rationale).
                 MANIFEST-section.MF's bytes were EXTRACTED from the actual
                 Ant-built jar's META-INF/MANIFEST.MF (unzip -p
                 modules/ui_data/jar/org.scilab.modules.ui_data.jar
                 META-INF/MANIFEST.MF), never retyped: Specification-Vendor
                 and Implementation-Vendor both carry the double-mangled
                 "Ã¨" (bytes c3 83 c2 a8) — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
                 fuller comment for the mechanism. Implementation-Version is
                 present, frozen at the literal "00000000 0000", positioned
                 between Implementation-Title and Implementation-Vendor
                 exactly where Ant places it. -->
            <manifestFile>${project.basedir}/src/main/manifest/MANIFEST-section.MF</manifestFile>
          </archive>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
